AXL001 app/Main.axl:11:46: error: `continue` can only be the handler of an `attempt` on a line of its own; to keep the value, keep the `Result`: `val r = attempt ... else e -> e.getMessage()`, then `if (r is Err) { continue }`, after which `r.value()` reads the value
AXL001 app/ReturnValue.axl:7:55: error: `return` can only be the handler of an `attempt` on a line of its own; to keep the value, keep the `Result`: `val r = attempt ... else e -> e.getMessage()`, then `if (r is Err) { return -1 }`, after which `r.value()` reads the value
AXL001 app/UseReturn.axl:9:17: error: the `else` of `use` is a call or a `throw`, not `return`; throw there, and handle the failure where the function is called: `attempt f() else e -> ...`
